    <statement><p>Evaluate the function at the specified points.</p>
<p><m>f(x,y) = y+xy^{2}, \left(-1,-3\right), \left(-1,2\right), \left(3,-5\right)</m></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-1,-3\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-1,2\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(3,-5\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-12</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>70</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>(x,y) = \left(-1,-3\right)</m> to find 
<m>f(-1,-3) = -3   - 1(-3)^{2} = -12</m>.



Similarly, with <m>(x,y) = \left(-1,2\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(-1,2) = 2   - 1(2)^{2} = -2</m>.



Finally, for <m>(x,y) = \left(3,-5\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(3,-5) = -5  + 3(-5)^{2} = 70</m>.


</solution>
